.TH TERMEXPLORER 1 "November 2026" "termexplorer 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termexplorer \- High-performance, keyboard-driven Linux developer workstation written in pure Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termexplorer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TermExplorer
is a lightweight, modal developer workstation for Unix terminals. It integrates a 2-pane workspace combining a 25% hierarchical filesystem explorer with a 75% inspector and previewer pane, an embedded PTY interactive shell drawer, native Git status and branch visualization, project-aware task runner, and a secure WebAssembly plugin sandbox.
.PP
When launched without arguments,
.B termexplorer
opens in the current working directory. If a \fIPATH\fR is provided and points to a directory, navigation initializes at that location.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print concise command-line help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the software version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-health
Run system diagnostics, inspect terminal TrueColor capabilities, detect Nerd Fonts, audit PTY subsystem availability, verify FreeDesktop Trash, check configuration paths, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-cwd\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Upon clean exit, write the last active working directory path into \fIPATH\fR. Useful for shell wrapper functions to change directory in the parent shell.
.TP
.BR \-\-chooser\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Upon clean exit, write the absolute path of the currently selected file or directory into \fIPATH\fR.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Navigation & Explorer
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBj\fR, \fBk\fR / \fBDown\fR, \fBUp\fR: Move selection down / up
.IP \(bu 2
\fBh\fR / \fBLeft\fR: Navigate to parent directory or collapse node
.IP \(bu 2
\fBl\fR / \fBRight\fR, \fBEnter\fR: Enter directory or expand node
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgg\fR / \fBG\fR: Jump to top / bottom of file tree
.IP \(bu 2
\fBzh\fR / \fB.\fR: Toggle hidden files display
.IP \(bu 2
\fB/\fR: Initiate real-time fuzzy filter within directory
.RE
.TP
.B Workstation & Panels
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTab\fR / \fBShift-Tab\fR: Cycle focus between Explorer, Preview, and Panels
.IP \(bu 2
\fB`\fR (Backtick) / \fBCtrl-`\fR: Toggle embedded PTY terminal drawer (15% height)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBctrl-p\fR: Open Command Palette
.IP \(bu 2
\fBg\fR: Open Git panel
.IP \(bu 2
\fBq\fR / \fBCtrl-c\fR: Exit TermExplorer
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Specifies the directory where user configuration is stored. Defaults to \fI~/.config\fR. TermExplorer loads its configuration from \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/termexplorer/config.toml\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Specifies the directory where persistent data, logs, and WebAssembly plugins reside. Defaults to \fI~/.local/share\fR. TermExplorer stores logs and plugins in \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/termexplorer\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Specifies the directory where cache files (e.g., syntax highlight cache, preview image renders) reside. Defaults to \fI~/.cache/termexplorer\fR.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
When set to \fItruecolor\fR or \fI24bit\fR, TermExplorer activates 24-bit RGB TrueColor rendering for Catppuccin Mocha and ANSI palette themes.
.TP
.B NERD_FONT
When set to \fI1\fR or \fItrue\fR, TermExplorer uses high-fidelity Nerd Font glyphs for file extensions, Git status, and UI icons. Otherwise, standard Unicode symbols and ASCII fallbacks are used.
.TP
.B SHELL
Specifies the default shell executed inside the embedded PTY terminal drawer. Defaults to \fI/bin/sh\fR if unset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/termexplorer/config.toml
Main application configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/termexplorer/termexplorer.log
Rolling diagnostic and application logs.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/termexplorer/plugins/
Directory containing compiled WebAssembly (.wasm) extensions.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/termexplorer/
Cached preview renders and syntax metadata.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime application error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments or missing option parameter.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch TermExplorer in current directory:
.B termexplorer
.TP
Inspect system environment and diagnostic health:
.B termexplorer --health
.TP
Open TermExplorer in a specific project directory:
.B termexplorer /path/to/project
.TP
Shell wrapper for automatic cd on exit (add to ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc):
.nf
termexplorer_cd() {
    local tmp="$(mktemp -t te-cwd.XXXXXX)"
    termexplorer --cwd-file="$tmp" "$@"
    if [ -f "$tmp" ]; then
        local dir="$(cat "$tmp")"
        rm -f "$tmp"
        [ -d "$dir" ] && [ "$dir" != "$PWD" ] && cd "$dir"
    fi
}
alias te=termexplorer_cd
.fi
